Desperately trying to break away, you attempt to take a hand-made machete out of the bag, but dreadful branches surround you from all sides, and every new movement is getting harder to make. Soon your arms and legs are tightly adhered to the plant.
The spots of skin uncovered by clothing begin to burn. At first a little, but then burning pain becomes intolerable. The wind muffles weak cry for help, and soon your body hangs upon the predatory branches, that drain your life greedily. Your adventure ends here.